{"type": "FeatureCollection", "metadata": {"note": "Montgomery, AL's other historic rail approach, from Nashville via Birmingham (see west_point_route_atlanta_montgomery.geojson for the Atlanta approach). The South & North Alabama Railroad, chartered in the 1850s but stalled by the Civil War, resumed construction in 1869; the Calera-Montgomery segment (63 miles) was complete by the end of 1870. The Louisville & Nashville Railroad took over the unfinished contract in 1871 and financed completion north to a crossing with the Alabama & Chattanooga Railroad -- the crossing that founded Birmingham itself in 1871 -- giving a through Nashville-Decatur-Birmingham-Montgomery line by 1872. This is the same L&N that built Montgomery's grand Union Station in 1898. The line's story has a clean ending: Amtrak's Floridian (Chicago-Nashville-Birmingham-Montgomery-Jacksonville, with branches to Miami and St. Petersburg) ran on ex-L&N trackage between Louisville and Montgomery from its Nov 14 1971 debut until it was discontinued Oct 9 1979 in a round of Carter-administration long-distance train cuts -- and that discontinuation is the same 1979 date Montgomery Union Station's own history gives for when all passenger rail service there ended. Geometry is a real-town waypoint approximation (Nashville-Decatur-Birmingham-Calera-Montgomery), straight-line segments between documented stations -- NOT digitized from period track maps.", "sources": ["https://www.bhamwiki.com/w/South_%26_North_Alabama_Railroad (chartered 1850s, stalled by the war; construction resumed 1869; Calera-Montgomery complete by end of 1870; L&N took over the unfinished contract 1871, financing the line north to the crossing that founded Birmingham 1871)", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgomery_Union_Station (L&N-built station opened 1898; rail service to the station ended 1979)", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floridian_(train,_1971%E2%80%931979) (Amtrak's Floridian ran Chicago-Florida Nov 14 1971-Oct 9 1979, on the L&N between Louisville and Montgomery, then Seaboard Coast Line trackage on to Jacksonville with Miami and St. Petersburg branches; discontinued after a US DOT study, having lost $21 million in 1978)"], "not_yet_sourced": "Exact frequency for any era, all estimated; whether any named train specifically branded the Nashville-Montgomery segment before the Floridian (e.g. an L&N-era predecessor), unconfirmed; precise date the South & North Alabama's Calera-Birmingham segment (vs. Calera-Montgomery) was completed.", "line_label_audit": "2026-08-24: line labels normalised repo-wide to \"<operating company>: <line name>\" -- the company's common display name (legal suffixes dropped), then the line as a passenger would have known it, or its two terminals where the line carried no advertised name. Long intermediate station lists were reduced to endpoints. For features spanning several operators the company shown is the one that ran the line for most of its drawn years. See CLAUDE.md Rule 6."}, "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Louisville and Nashville Railroad (South & North Alabama Railroad)", "line": "Louisville and Nashville: Nashville \u2013 Montgomery", "id": "ln-nashville-birmingham-montgomery", "color": "#7A4419", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 50, "speed_source": "estimated: blended across the line's history; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1872, "end": 1971, "headway_min": 480, "note": "South & North Alabama Railroad's Calera-Montgomery segment complete by end of 1870; L&N financed completion north through the crossing that founded Birmingham (1871), giving a through Nashville-Decatur-Birmingham-Montgomery line by 1872; L&N built Montgomery's Union Station in 1898; frequency estimated/unsourced", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://www.bhamwiki.com/w/South_%26_North_Alabama_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgomery_Union_Station", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floridian_(train"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-86.7511, 33.1043], "to": [-86.3, 32.3792], "chord_mi": 56.38, "traced_mi": 64.35, "snap_m": [29, 728], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["CSX S&NA South Subdivision (60.18 mi)", "(rail) (3.03 mi)", "(disused) [disused] (1.03 mi)", "(abandoned) [abandoned] (0.07 mi)", "CoG [disused] (0.03 mi)", "CSX M&M Subdivision (0.01 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.5 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-86.7511, 33.1043], "to": [-86.3, 32.3792], "chord_mi": 56.38, "traced_mi": 64.35, "snap_m": [29, 728], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["CSX S&NA South Subdivision (60.18 mi)", "(rail) (3.03 mi)", "(disused) [disused] (1.03 mi)", "(abandoned) [abandoned] (0.07 mi)", "CoG [disused] (0.03 mi)", "CSX M&M Subdivision (0.01 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.5 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-86.8421, 33.4953], "to": [-86.7511, 33.1043], "chord_mi": 27.51, "traced_mi": 34.66, "snap_m": [4, 29], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["CSX S&NA South Subdivision (20.78 mi)", "CSX Boyles Terminal Subdivision (12.01 mi)", "NS AGS South District (1.83 mi)", "(rail) (0.04 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}], "geometry_quality": "Straight-line repair 2026-08-29: 1 ruled segment totalling 56 mi replaced with OpenStreetMap-traced rail geometry (see geometry_repairs for the OSM lines each one followed). Straight-line repair 2026-08-29: 3 ruled segments totalling 140 mi replaced with OpenStreetMap-traced rail geometry (see geometry_repairs for the OSM lines each one followed)."}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-86.7816, 36.1627], [-86.9878, 34.6059], [-86.8421, 33.4953], [-